    "text": "To solve the problem, we first need to determine how many marbles each person initially has based on the given ratio 3:5:7. The total number of marbles is 600.\n\nThe ratio 3:5:7 means that the total parts of the ratio are \\(3 + 5 + 7 = 15\\). Therefore, each part of the ratio represents \\(\\frac{600}{15} = 40\\) marbles.\n\n- Brittany has \\(3 \\times 40 = 120\\) marbles.\n- Alex has \\(5 \\times 40 = 200\\) marbles.\n- Jamy has \\(7 \\times 40 = 280\\) marbles.\n\nNext, Brittany gives Alex half of her marbles. So, Brittany gives Alex \\(\\frac{120}{2} = 60\\) marbles.\n\nAfter receiving these 60 marbles, Alex now has \\(200 + 60 = 260\\) marbles.\n\nTherefore, the total number of marbles that Alex has is \\(\\boxed{260}\\).",
